WEBVTT

00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:03.750
Get away!

00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:13.210
Get away!

00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:24.120
This is not the great word.

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:39.870
What's going on here?

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:44.240
This wasn't the great word waiting to be born inside the whirling vortex, right?

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:46.980
Why did another word come out?

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:52.310
It's Subete. His will changed the word.

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:54.920
Verbalize.

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:57.480
I can do it. I can do this.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:03.790
"Separation"

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:08.800
Big Brother Hayato!

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:10.460
We're doing it, Karan!

00:01:09.430 --> 00:01:10.100
"Hayato Kujyo" "Karan Uminagi"

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:13.770
Uzu!

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:16.840
"Wings of the Calm Wind"

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:22.280
Wings of the Calm Wind!

00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:21.340
"Wings of the Calm Wind"

00:01:35.290 --> 00:01:36.790
We did it, Big Brother!

00:01:36.790 --> 00:01:39.860
He just <i>had</i> to keep us on the edge of our seats.

00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:43.030
Wait, this is...!

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:45.760
What? This isn't how it normally is!

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:55.040
What is that?!

00:01:55.040 --> 00:01:57.640
Tornado Strike!

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:09.050
We'll settle this, Akira Kaibuki.

00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:14.800
At one time, man was one with the world of truth.

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:20.370
But the written word brought forth prosperity and suffering.

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:29.580
<i>Oh, "yamai-dare," darlin' darlin,'</i> <i>you're a divine crown</i>

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:35.580
<i>The kanji for "love" and "grief " look very similar</i>

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:40.990
<i>When I realized that, dawn suddenly broke</i>

00:02:40.990 --> 00:02:46.760
<i>The air was filled with so much</i> <i>silence that "blue" "fought"</i>

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:53.100
<i>When suddenly you slid in to the right of me</i>

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:56.000
<i>Rippling with a clatter</i>

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:58.940
<i>and tangled in red thread</i>

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:03.850
<i>and a 39-degree fever of passion</i>

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:09.280
<i>Oh, "yamai-dare," darlin' darlin,'</i> <i>you're a divine crown</i>

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:15.360
<i>A crown worn on high with pride</i>

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:20.800
<i>Oh, "yamai-dare," darlin' darlin,'</i> <i>"soothe" my hidden "heart below"</i>

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:26.800
<i>Its form is too much to handle right now</i>

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:29.740
<i>God's wisdom, the "h" in "her"</i>

00:03:29.740 --> 00:03:32.470
<i>With a tearful, feverish gaze</i>

00:03:32.470 --> 00:03:35.410
<i>let's stand side by side</i> <i>and look at tomorrow's moon</i>

00:03:35.410 --> 00:03:38.250
<i>(Let's stand side by side</i> <i>and look at tomorrow's moon)</i>

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:45.650
<i>The things you can do are so striking</i>

00:03:50.430 --> 00:03:53.730
"Bring Them Together! Heart and Heart"

00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:54.100
Unlocking duct barrel.

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:57.100
Raising electromagnetic catapult deck output by five points per second.

00:03:57.100 --> 00:03:58.830
Skies are clear above Asagaya Station.

00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:02.100
Thruster charging will complete in another 25 seconds.

00:04:02.100 --> 00:04:06.010
Vectors 1, 2, and 3, launch on the double.

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:10.450
We had no clue another
M.J.B.K. space had opened.

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:12.410
How did we fail to detect it?

00:04:12.410 --> 00:04:14.650
Probably because of the whirl M.J.B.K.

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:18.180
I think there was interference in our Field Detection System.

00:04:19.450 --> 00:04:22.620
Subete, you...

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:24.180
Verbalize.

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:33.600
Blue and pink crafts... It's not him.

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:35.090
In that case...

00:04:38.610 --> 00:04:40.670
...I'll just have to drag him out!

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:47.980
An ability to attack by splitting off a part of his body?

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:51.110
It's dangerous, but if we can just close in...

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:55.620
We're gonna cut right through you!

00:05:00.130 --> 00:05:02.960
Don't get so touchy-feely! Stay back!

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:11.340
Long-range attacks and close-range deflection?

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:13.540
So that's how it is...

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:19.170
Here they come.

00:05:22.820 --> 00:05:24.320
Sousei Gattai.

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:25.650
Shine!

00:05:25.650 --> 00:05:29.350
Aquarion...

00:05:38.570 --> 00:05:40.230
...Angel!

00:05:38.830 --> 00:05:39.930
"Angel"

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:49.680
Be careful! That thing can manipulate distance at will!

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:52.080
D-Distance?

00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:54.680
Tornado Strike!

00:06:12.570 --> 00:06:14.230
He bounced it back!

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:33.280
Above you, Kaibuki!

00:06:39.730 --> 00:06:43.130
Subete! What are you fighting for?

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:47.500
Have you thought about what it means to erase words from this world?

00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:51.440
Red Vector, Akira Kaibuki, you get away!

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:53.470
Get away from Maia!

00:06:54.480 --> 00:06:55.270
"Separation"

00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:06.790
Wh-What?

00:07:06.790 --> 00:07:08.280
Dodge it!

00:07:12.790 --> 00:07:16.800
Th-They're moving away from me...

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:19.800
The things that matter to me... My dreams...

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:22.270
Kokone Kikogami! Pull yourself together!

00:07:23.270 --> 00:07:25.170
A psychological attack, huh?

00:07:25.170 --> 00:07:28.510
N-No! W-We're coming apart!

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:37.050
Their Gattai's been broken!

00:07:44.990 --> 00:07:46.480
Karan!

00:07:50.700 --> 00:07:55.730
I understand now. I can see your hearts through the M.J.B.K.

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:02.240
You're all separate!

00:08:05.850 --> 00:08:08.480
We can't fight like this!

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:09.880
Pull back for now.

00:08:09.880 --> 00:08:13.020
Fortunately, the word corrosion rate isn't rising quickly.

00:08:13.020 --> 00:08:17.220
We should have time to pull back and regroup.

00:08:19.730 --> 00:08:23.230
What are you doing? Hurry back, Akira!

00:08:23.230 --> 00:08:27.370
He is a threat to the world.
I cannot leave him unchecked!

00:08:27.370 --> 00:08:29.170
This is crazy, Akira!

00:08:37.710 --> 00:08:39.270
Akira...

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:42.340
Get away!

00:08:48.290 --> 00:08:51.460
Everyone has... been split up.

00:08:51.460 --> 00:08:54.860
I will end this, Akira Kaibuki!

00:09:12.650 --> 00:09:15.720
Hayato... Kujyo...

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:19.740
I merely followed the optimal strategy...

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:24.960
Force withdraw all vectors! Now!

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:26.450
Y-Yes, ma'am!

00:09:34.770 --> 00:09:36.290
I won't let you go.

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:43.640
I've exhausted too much of my Verbalism Ability.

00:09:43.640 --> 00:09:46.310
But... I learned something here.

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:49.310
I... can beat you...

00:09:55.660 --> 00:09:58.290
Are you and the others all okay now, Maia?

00:09:58.290 --> 00:09:59.490
Yeah.

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:03.530
It seems the M.J.B.K.'s psychological attack was a temporary thing.

00:10:03.530 --> 00:10:05.670
It's not having an effect anymore.

00:10:05.670 --> 00:10:07.360
On us, at least.

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:10.940
Big Brother...

00:10:10.940 --> 00:10:17.380
I-It's because I got taken out so fast... because of me...

00:10:17.380 --> 00:10:19.050
No.

00:10:19.050 --> 00:10:23.350
Are you so egotistical that you'd put your own comrades' lives at risk?

00:10:26.320 --> 00:10:27.850
Akira...

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:42.330
Oh, there he is!

00:10:45.010 --> 00:10:47.130
"Separation"

00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:52.710
"Separation"

00:10:48.740 --> 00:10:53.750
Right now, there doesn't seem to be any major damage from the M.J.B.K.

00:10:53.750 --> 00:10:57.650
The word corrosion rate has only risen 1% over the course of two hours.

00:10:57.650 --> 00:10:59.550
So some of them are like this, huh?

00:10:59.550 --> 00:11:03.090
No change to gravity potential of enemy inside M.J.B.K. space.

00:11:03.090 --> 00:11:06.730
--It has ceased moving, as well.
--Oh, my shoulders are stiff.

00:11:06.730 --> 00:11:09.230
You should get some rest yourself.

00:11:09.230 --> 00:11:11.730
I will, thank you.

00:11:11.730 --> 00:11:14.540
Since the Vectors can't launch until they're repaired,

00:11:14.540 --> 00:11:16.440
this stagnation is saving us.

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:18.740
But I'm concerned that I don't know the reason for it...

00:11:22.610 --> 00:11:27.450
He may be the one chosen by Verbalism.

00:11:29.920 --> 00:11:33.620
You could never win against the chosen one, anyway.

00:11:33.620 --> 00:11:36.190
Not against that man in that red Vector.

00:11:36.190 --> 00:11:39.030
No! The chosen one is...!

00:11:39.030 --> 00:11:44.870
He's suppressing the M.J.B.K.'s power while maintaining his fusion with it.

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:48.100
By doing so, in exchange for the word corrosion rate stagnating,

00:11:48.100 --> 00:11:50.970
he can reduce the strain on his body.

00:11:50.970 --> 00:11:54.410
That's pretty impressive, don't you think?

00:11:54.410 --> 00:12:00.750
The word Subete has brought forth was transformed from the great word.

00:12:00.750 --> 00:12:04.050
But the change is incomplete.

00:12:04.050 --> 00:12:07.890
If his psyche shows weakness here...

00:12:07.890 --> 00:12:11.660
If that happens, Subete,

00:12:11.660 --> 00:12:16.600
can you pull the trigger that will change the world?

00:12:21.740 --> 00:12:25.670
There's something big out there. Is it coming?

00:12:25.670 --> 00:12:28.240
No, is it sleeping?

00:12:28.240 --> 00:12:29.900
I can't tell.

00:12:33.450 --> 00:12:34.940
Who's there?

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:44.760
Akira! Why are you here?

00:12:44.760 --> 00:12:46.360
Want some?

00:12:46.360 --> 00:12:51.200
What are you doing here?
You were told to go home for now.

00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:54.540
There's no telling when we'll have to head out.

00:12:54.540 --> 00:12:57.030
It's more efficient for me to stay here.

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:04.550
What?

00:13:04.550 --> 00:13:08.380
Is what happened to
Hayato Kujyo bothering you?

00:13:10.550 --> 00:13:12.820
There was something he said.

00:13:12.820 --> 00:13:15.690
"What do you mean when you say you're the savior?

00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:18.990
What do you want from the world you'll save?"

00:13:20.690 --> 00:13:23.130
There's nothing.

00:13:23.130 --> 00:13:26.900
A savior is one who saves the world.

00:13:26.900 --> 00:13:31.010
The reason why, and what comes afterwards...

00:13:31.010 --> 00:13:33.670
I'd never thought about that.

00:13:33.670 --> 00:13:37.550
So, I tried thinking about it...

00:13:37.550 --> 00:13:39.580
There was nothing.

00:13:39.580 --> 00:13:45.750
Why are you so hung up on the idea of being a savior?

00:13:45.750 --> 00:13:47.560
I don't know.

00:13:47.560 --> 00:13:51.860
Still, I must be a savior.

00:13:51.860 --> 00:13:54.500
No matter what happens.

00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:59.230
The savior... It's my... My only...

00:14:02.400 --> 00:14:06.900
"Closed Due to Emergency

00:14:02.400 --> 00:14:06.900
Sorry. Come again another time!"

00:14:02.770 --> 00:14:04.410
Akira?

00:14:08.840 --> 00:14:10.330
Hey!

00:14:12.510 --> 00:14:14.570
I can smell Akira.

00:14:31.630 --> 00:14:34.570
Let go of me! That hurts!

00:14:34.570 --> 00:14:36.040
Let go!

00:14:36.040 --> 00:14:37.400
Akira, stop this at once.

00:14:37.400 --> 00:14:39.770
Get in your Vector. We're launching.

00:14:39.770 --> 00:14:43.910
Launch? The Vectors aren't fixed yet!

00:14:43.910 --> 00:14:45.880
Neither yours or Karan's!

00:14:45.880 --> 00:14:47.380
Not a problem. They'll move.

00:14:47.380 --> 00:14:49.780
Ow! That hurts!

00:14:49.780 --> 00:14:51.590
Akira, stop!

00:14:51.590 --> 00:14:54.420
Do you have a strategy for beating that M.J.B.K.?

00:14:54.420 --> 00:14:59.060
How do you plan to get through this with Gattai as good as useless?

00:14:59.060 --> 00:15:01.430
I'll think about that once we get there.

00:15:01.430 --> 00:15:05.830
Worst comes to worst, we crash any unusable Vectors into the enemy.

00:15:07.800 --> 00:15:09.740
What are you saying?

00:15:09.740 --> 00:15:12.470
Whoever's piloting it won't get off unharmed if you do that!

00:15:12.470 --> 00:15:13.770
Yeah, and?

00:15:13.770 --> 00:15:17.640
If they're in the way of saving the world, obviously I'd sacrifice them.

00:15:18.850 --> 00:15:20.510
Are you serious?!

00:15:20.510 --> 00:15:24.920
A-Akira...! You're joking, right?

00:15:24.920 --> 00:15:30.490
Y-You wouldn't actually think that, r-right?

00:15:30.490 --> 00:15:32.930
We lost because of you.

00:15:34.530 --> 00:15:36.860
If you're going to get in my way, get lost.

00:15:36.860 --> 00:15:39.270
Y-You can't mean that...

00:15:39.270 --> 00:15:41.140
Cut it out already!

00:15:41.140 --> 00:15:43.300
Hayato Kujyo is of no further use.

00:15:43.300 --> 00:15:46.310
So, Karan Uminagi, you come with me.

00:15:46.310 --> 00:15:50.210
No use? What's that supposed to mean? Take that back!

00:15:50.210 --> 00:15:53.180
Shut up and do as I say. For I am...

00:15:53.180 --> 00:15:55.170
You jerk!

00:15:57.380 --> 00:16:00.890
I won't allow you to use the Vectors like your own personal property.

00:16:00.890 --> 00:16:03.190
Take Akira Kaibuki to the holding cells.

00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:08.890
What's gotten into you?

00:16:18.710 --> 00:16:20.970
Akira, you...

00:16:30.520 --> 00:16:33.590
Akira... why?

00:16:33.590 --> 00:16:35.320
Who cares?

00:16:42.430 --> 00:16:44.230
Stupid Akira!

00:16:55.240 --> 00:16:56.730
It's time for the second round.

00:16:59.010 --> 00:17:00.680
--Large pulse detected near M.J.B.K.
--Energy link to Logos World detected.

00:17:00.680 --> 00:17:04.690
M.J.B.K. influence detected in
Deava base. This is dangerous.

00:17:04.690 --> 00:17:05.790
What happened?

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:09.190
Word corrosion rate has begun to rise rapidly!

00:17:09.190 --> 00:17:10.680
What?

00:17:13.360 --> 00:17:16.930
Why? I'm sure I was in my room.

00:17:16.930 --> 00:17:19.270
Huh?

00:17:19.270 --> 00:17:22.630
Huh? I thought I was at Shirobaco...

00:17:27.910 --> 00:17:29.930
Why?!

00:17:31.080 --> 00:17:34.920
The next thing you noticed, you were in Asakusa? Are you half asleep?

00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:38.650
That's not it, you dolt! I'm wide awake!

00:17:38.650 --> 00:17:42.090
Anyway, I'm heading right back, so pay my train fare for me!

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:43.490
"Tokyo Performance Hall"

00:17:44.390 --> 00:17:47.560
Huh? Didn't I just pass by here?

00:17:51.300 --> 00:17:54.100
I-I-I'm back here?

00:17:54.100 --> 00:17:56.800
I need to hurry back to everyone else!

00:17:59.010 --> 00:18:01.100
What's with this endless loop?!

00:18:02.340 --> 00:18:04.910
Why can't I see Shirobaco?

00:18:04.910 --> 00:18:07.850
The M.J.B.K.'s effect? But why?

00:18:07.850 --> 00:18:09.910
If there's one reason I can think of...

00:18:15.290 --> 00:18:16.850
Hey, you...

00:18:20.930 --> 00:18:22.450
Verbalize.

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:28.460
Hey, you can't do that!
We aren't done fixing it!

00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:33.340
Vector-1 launched!

00:18:33.340 --> 00:18:34.540
I thought so.

00:18:34.540 --> 00:18:39.180
He used the M.J.B.K.'s power to distance himself from the others.

00:18:39.180 --> 00:18:40.180
To distance himself?

00:18:40.180 --> 00:18:42.650
Because he pushed us away,

00:18:42.650 --> 00:18:45.620
there was an emotional distance between Akira and everyone else.

00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:48.520
The M.J.B.K. took advantage of that,

00:18:48.520 --> 00:18:51.660
and the emotional distance was translated into physical distance.

00:18:51.660 --> 00:18:54.130
Why would he do that?

00:18:54.130 --> 00:18:59.200
Most likely so he could fight alone, without getting the others involved.

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:01.840
So that was it.

00:19:01.840 --> 00:19:04.240
That idiot! That idiot!

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:08.180
I thought there must be some reason for his sudden attitude, but...

00:19:08.180 --> 00:19:10.640
But I didn't think he'd take it this far.

00:19:10.640 --> 00:19:14.550
But there's no way he can beat a M.J.B.K. with just one Vector.

00:19:14.550 --> 00:19:17.520
It's not that Akira doesn't understand that.

00:19:17.520 --> 00:19:20.920
So I'm sure that, deep inside, he's waiting.

00:19:20.920 --> 00:19:25.720
For someone who'll still try to close the gap between them.

00:19:28.230 --> 00:19:30.760
You idiot! You stupid idiot!

00:19:30.760 --> 00:19:34.360
I've never learned how to give up!

00:19:40.340 --> 00:19:43.110
Diving at me yourself? Are you a moron?

00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:50.750
Subete Kenzaki, do you know the etymology of the "separation" kanji?

00:19:50.180 --> 00:19:51.620
"Separation"

00:19:50.750 --> 00:19:52.720
It's a bird and snake.

00:19:52.720 --> 00:19:55.760
The two intertwined and couldn't be separated.

00:19:55.760 --> 00:19:58.450
That's one theory on how this kanji came to be.

00:19:59.460 --> 00:20:03.360
So I will become the bird and cut this kanji away!

00:20:08.400 --> 00:20:11.960
Trying to break my kanji into its constituent parts? It won't work!

00:20:13.640 --> 00:20:17.210
No! He can't draw out enough of his Verbalism Ability in a Vector!

00:20:17.210 --> 00:20:19.740
Give it up! I've won!

00:20:22.880 --> 00:20:24.370
Maia?

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:29.090
What are you doing, Maia? It's done now.

00:20:29.090 --> 00:20:33.930
Akira Kaibuki is gone.
You can come back to me.

00:20:33.930 --> 00:20:36.630
Can you hear me, Akira?

00:20:36.630 --> 00:20:38.400
Communications?

00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:41.470
Am I hearing them through the red Vector I swallowed?

00:20:41.470 --> 00:20:44.500
You're always so arbitrary.

00:20:44.500 --> 00:20:47.470
I could never let you go alone.

00:20:47.470 --> 00:20:51.010
I chose to go with you.

00:20:51.010 --> 00:20:54.280
Maia, why?

00:20:53.310 --> 00:20:58.690
"Voice ID

00:20:53.310 --> 00:20:58.690
Maia Tsukigane"

00:20:54.280 --> 00:20:58.820
I've finally realized you're the only one for me.

00:20:58.820 --> 00:21:04.420
Yes, since that time, Subete just wouldn't do. It has to be you!

00:21:04.420 --> 00:21:06.960
What... are you saying?

00:21:06.960 --> 00:21:10.020
I want to Gattai with you!

00:21:13.970 --> 00:21:14.660
"Join"

00:21:19.810 --> 00:21:22.610
Akira!

00:21:25.450 --> 00:21:26.710
Stop!

00:21:26.710 --> 00:21:31.850
No! Get away! Get away! Get away from her!

00:21:32.890 --> 00:21:35.020
Sousei Gattai.

00:21:35.020 --> 00:21:37.460
Shout!

00:21:37.460 --> 00:21:40.790
Aquarion!

00:21:46.470 --> 00:21:50.740
Yes, I could never be separated from you.

00:21:50.740 --> 00:21:55.400
Because... this feels so good!

00:22:02.150 --> 00:22:03.320
"Kou"

00:22:02.250 --> 00:22:03.750
Kou!

00:22:13.360 --> 00:22:17.500
Akira Kaibuki!

00:22:17.500 --> 00:22:20.160
I will end this, Subete Kenzaki.

00:22:37.420 --> 00:22:40.890
<i>Je-Je t'aime communication</i>

00:22:40.890 --> 00:22:50.890
<i>Oh, you aren't making a bit of</i> <i>eye contact with me while you talk</i>

00:22:50.930 --> 00:23:00.140
<i>Are you texting some far-off</i> <i>neighboring world or something?</i>

00:23:00.140 --> 00:23:05.270
<i>Because this isn't communication at all</i>

00:23:07.210 --> 00:23:13.750
<i>You'd at least understand that much</i>

00:23:13.750 --> 00:23:19.760
<i>even if the times suddenly changed, right?</i>

00:23:19.760 --> 00:23:23.760
<i>Give me je t'aime communication sometimes</i>

00:23:23.760 --> 00:23:27.170
<i>Look at me, answer me, and tell me</i>

00:23:27.170 --> 00:23:33.670
<i>I mean, this is practically</i> <i>like talking to a computer</i>

00:23:33.670 --> 00:23:36.680
<i>A-Adieu application</i>

00:23:36.680 --> 00:23:43.320
<i>Even if it means staying lonely</i> <i>in my heart, if it'll connect us</i>

00:23:43.320 --> 00:23:49.690
<i>then, please, at least show</i> <i>your smile to me alone</i>

00:23:51.460 --> 00:23:52.930
I've got the paper decorations ready!

00:23:52.930 --> 00:23:55.600
I want to try throwing someone in the air!

00:23:55.600 --> 00:23:58.200
--What are you talking about?
--I've already bought a daruma doll!

00:23:58.200 --> 00:23:59.770
I'll draw in the eyes!

00:23:59.770 --> 00:24:01.440
We're ready for the launch!

00:24:01.440 --> 00:24:03.700
H-Hold on, everyone, you're getting carried away.

00:24:03.700 --> 00:24:05.510
Next time: Episode 13.

00:24:04.200 --> 00:24:07.710
"Episode 13: A Great Victory! Our Savior"

00:24:05.510 --> 00:24:08.040
"A Great Victory! Our Savior."

00:24:08.040 --> 00:24:10.810
Do you think... we can win?
